{"GroupPermissionsV2.canManage() checks both VIEW and MANAGE scopes, allowing users with only VIEW permission to pass the manage authorization check, which is a privilege escalation": 0.9697997570037842, "In GroupPermissionsV2.getGroupIdsWithViewPermission(), groupResource.getId() (the internal authorization resource store UUID) is used instead of groupResource.getName() (the actual group ID), breaking both the per-resource permission lookup and the returned set of group IDs": 0.9826463460922241, "GroupPermissionsV2.hasPermission() can throw NullPointerException when neither a per-group resource exists nor the fallback resource-type resource (name 'Groups') exists, because it calls policyStore.findByResource(server, resource) with a potentially null resource": 0.9389709830284119, "AdminPermissionsSchema.getOrCreateResource() creates per-group resources without setting Resource.type, but GroupPermissionsV2.getGroupIdsWithViewPermission() enumerates group resources via resourceStore.findByType(server, 'Groups'), causing enumeration to return no per-group resources": 0.9164557456970215, "The canView() guard was removed before setting the UserModel.GROUPS session attribute, causing grantIfNoPermission to be set to true even when the caller already has full view access, which can lead to incorrect permission grants": 0.46463489532470703, "In GroupResourceTypeEvaluationTest.onBefore(), the Response is closed by try-with-resources and then ApiUtil.handleCreatedResponse(response) also closes it internally, resulting in a double-close of the JAX-RS Response object": 0.7925951480865479}